{"data": [{"author_id": "1363408102624808961", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:09:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117423980273701360"], "id": "2117423980273701360", "lang": "pt", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno @suno vocês continuam pegando ideias de usuários como eu que crio lá dentro e passando as ideias para outros usuários ? Nesta atualização você mudou isso ?", "url": "https://x.com/fernand88947533/status/2117423980273701360"}, {"author_id": "2114099588000817152", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:47:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117418417896775748"], "id": "2117418417896775748", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@GordonF38802537 @suno Recording guitar? Keep a clean DI track alongside your amp sound.\n\nIf the tone sounds wrong next week, you re-amp that DI through a different amp or sim instead of replaying the take.\n\nCommit to the performance. Keep the tone negotiable.", "url": "https://x.com/ctrlshiftmike/status/2117418417896775748"}, {"author_id": "823586771959058432", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:05:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117407855271653818"], "id": "2117407855271653818", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno The important feedback: do something about the awful synthetic electric guitar sound. You know the one. The one that makes it obvious that the song is AI. It doesn't sound like a hand playing the guitar.\n\nhttps://t.co/K8kx0Rt72z", "url": "https://x.com/Denise_TEW2013/status/2117407855271653818"}, {"author_id": "29409629", "conversati