y do a song cut off midway through the track when songs doesn’t.", "url": "https://x.com/awykked/status/2117351579980550244"}, {"author_id": "107152604", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:53:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117344435646406780"], "id": "2117344435646406780", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 99, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno My lyrics \nMy beats \nMastered by Suno https://t.co/8kggq0zc7h", "url": "https://x.com/oka_iko/status/2117344435646406780"}, {"author_id": "1278442698417090564", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:43:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117341875233505722"], "id": "2117341875233505722", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 65, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno I've told you that the audio mix drifts on most of my uploaded home demos.\nV5.5 could render consistent sounding versions - V6 produces tracks where the drums and bass guitar change EQ and levels after about 2 minutes.\nThis results in repeated unusable versions.\nFIX THAT FLAW!", "url": "https://x.com/GordonF38802537/status/2117341875233505722"}, {"author_id": "1192226171888508935", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:46:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117327538175279318"], "id": "2117327538175279318", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 85, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "@suno No, we told you to give us access to old versions like 5.5, 3, and 2, etc.", "url": "https://x.com/Brotherhoodoft5/status/2117327538175279318"}, {"author_id": "1744851881493508096", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:44:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117326896543179039"], "id": "2117326896543179039", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno we also told you that we loved 4.5+.. Did you listen? No, you took it away", "url": "https://x.com/meeekaaaahhh/status/2117326896543179039"}, {"author_id": "2078545678478053377", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:36:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117324907835162813"], "id": "2117324907835162813", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 64, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno how about working on audio degenerating past 1m 30s?\nyou know, the shit that's been plaguing us since fucking chirp 2", "url": "https://x.com/SolipsRenatus/status/2117324907835162813"}, {"author_id": "920170929019240448", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:26:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117322564116852821"], "id": "2117322564116852821", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Great update. Everything in one place makes editing much easier.", "url": "https://x.com/HanaFutureAI/status/2117322564116852821"}, {"author_id": "1276283406", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T18:05:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117317246540521856"], "id": "2117317246540521856", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 78, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno @suno Add an option to choose whether or not to include a \"reverb\" effect in our creations, before starting the generation process! In V6, having all this \"reverb\" on the voice by default is really annoying.", "url": "https://x.com/MonsieurSeby/status/2117317246540521856"}, {"author_id": "2066309377842155520", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:29:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117308032342221200"], "id": "2117308032342221200", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Fine pitch is the one I'll use most for tightening my vocals\n\nNext ask- cleaner stem separation, bleed cleanup is still half my Studio time🫡`", "url": "https://x.com/BlackOuttheCEO/status/2117308032342221200"}, {"author_id": "1658947174267252736", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:03:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301670233182398"], "id": "2117301670233182398", "lang": "tr", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 76, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Sayın @MikeyShulman, geri bildirimmiş, sevsinler sizi. Suno Editor Beta sürümünü hala geliştirmediğiniz için, şarkılardaki hataları gidermek adına, seçili alanda benzerini üretme seçeneğini kaldırdığınız için, müzik dünyasının düşmanısınız Herkes Studio'yu kullanmak zorunda değil", "url": "https://x.com/AlpayUrludag/status/2117301670233182398"}, {"author_id": "2010151863572934657", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:54:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117299195757711790"], "id": "2117299195757711790", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 107, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Studio on tablet devices like iPad pro would be peak! I travel a ton and don't always have a laptop or desktop at the ready to work from the WebApps. Would love to see more of the features available on the go.", "url": "https://x.com/h3x0r_von_pr00t/status/2117299195757711790"}, {"author_id": "1948148806769582080", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:45:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117297043538600423"], "id": "2117297043538600423", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 124, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Thank you for the update. Will you allow users to export songs to a selected workspace soon?", "url": "https://x.com/5150_Asylum/status/2117297043538600423"}, {"author_id": "2004326215944196096", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:42:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117296404976832798"], "id": "2117296404976832798", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 167, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Consider eventually creating a slider for every stat, I was thinking about that last night when I was messing around with settings and realized that if you have two corresponding styles, you can obviously raise and lower those styles together, but not singularly.\n\nExample:\n\nLike https://t.co/VsxTen8wfU", "url": "https://x.com/AIEmmy348019/status/2117296404976832798"}, {"author_id": "765510712433213440", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:39:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117295658252283930"], "id": "2117295658252283930", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 111, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno Make volume automation adjustments right on track like in audition. It's much better than have it separately down below", "url": "https://x.com/Targeeks/status/2117295658252283930"}, {"author_id": "1095583300536561664", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:35:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117294518089490713"], "id": "2117294518089490713", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 156, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno I’m a fairly dedicated SUNO user, but ever since the update to Version 6, I haven’t been able to create a single track that I’m truly satisfied with. The reason is that most tracks have annoying little crackling or popping noises somewhere in the audio.\n\nThe track below is a", "url": "https://x.com/TigerGyroscope/status/2117294518089490713"}, {"author_id": "2110889476981460992", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:27:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117292430609584235"], "id": "2117292430609584235", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 101, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno bigger clip settings is a quiet win. most of my studio time goes into nudging one clip's start and end, not making new ones", "url": "https://x.com/luketestsai/status/2117292430609584235"}, {"author_id": "1706039547983749120", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:24:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117291739199541374"], "id": "2117291739199541374", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 99, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno bro can you pls respond to that support ticket i sent you regarding the illegitimate charge on my card ty", "url": "https://x.com/gh0stpen/status/2117291739199541374"}, {"author_id": "2063608391663063040", "conversation_id": "2117290720130449637", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:23:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117291477755900355"], "id": "2117291477755900355", "lang": "qme", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 89, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@suno 🔥", "ur